From 2838f3bf26c610a711a0b3d4025ac8dbcf5b91a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:10:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stats: count duplicates for the same records as "sequences";
 include isize 0 in the SD

"reads duplicated" and "bases duplicated" were accumulated before the
IS_ORIGINAL() gate in collect_stats(), so secondary and supplementary
records carrying the 0x400 flag were counted, while "sequences" and
"total length" exclude those records.  A duplication rate formed from the
two lines (MultiQC's samtools stats module does this) was therefore
overstated whenever the supplementary records of duplicates were flagged,
which is what `samtools markdup -S` and Picard MarkDuplicates produce.  On
the test input (20 reads, 8 duplicates, 4 supplementary records belonging
to duplicate pairs) the old code reported 10 duplicated reads out of 20
sequences; the new code reports 8.  The counting now happens inside the
IS_ORIGINAL() block, next to the read length counts.

The "insert size standard deviation" loop started at isize 1, while the
mean and the count used from isize 0 included the isize 0 bin.  Pairs
reported with TLEN 0 therefore entered the denominator but not the sum of
squares, so they lowered the standard deviation instead of raising it.  On
the test input (10 pairs, two with TLEN 0, the rest 300 to 360) the old
code reported an SD of 60.1 against a mean of 259.0; the correct value is
130.5.  The loop now starts at 0.

Two regression tests cover the two cases; both fail on the previous code.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
